# Domain boundaries

- Keep physical calculations in `domain/energy` and financial calculations in `domain/finance`.
- Finance consumes energy results and tariff schedules as values.
- A new Swiss dataset is a new adapter behind an existing port.
- Register the adapter in `composition.py` and settings. Leave the service unchanged.
- Quantities include a unit. Results include assumptions and an engine version.
- Store prices, tariffs, subsidies, and engineering assumptions as data or assumption-set fields.
- Scope assessment reads by organization id.
- Store future geometry as SRID 2056. Accept WGS84 at the API edge.
- The mock adapters stay free of surveyed yields, tariff rates, and subsidy amounts.

See `docs/calculations.md` and `docs/swiss-providers.md`.
